# `std::io::buf_io` — Buffered Stream Channel (`BufChannel` / `BufReader` + `BufWriter`)

## 1. Architectural Intent & Rust `std::io::{BufReader, BufWriter}` Comparison
In Rust (`std::io::BufReader` and `BufWriter`), internal buffer watermarks (`pos` and `filled`) are private fields maintained via manual `consume(amt)` and `fill_buf()` calls, where off-by-one watermark updates can corrupt stream framing.

In Jenny's `std::io::buf_io`, `BufChannel` unifies buffered framing atop `std::mem::raw_buf::RawBuf` and enforces the structural invariant `self.read_pos >= 0 && self.read_pos <= self.write_pos && self.write_pos <= self.buf.cap && self.flushed_count >= 0`, with `compact()` shifting unread frames to offset `0` via `RawBuf.copy_within`.

```jenny
module std_io_buf_io

import std::mem::raw_buf

pub enum BufIoError {
    BufferUnderflow,
    CapacityOverflow,
    InvalidFrame,
}

pub struct BufChannel {
    buf: RawBuf,
    read_pos: i64 = 0,
    write_pos: i64 = 0,
    flushed_count: i64 = 0,

    invariant self.read_pos >= 0 && self.read_pos <= self.write_pos && self.write_pos <= self.buf.cap && self.flushed_count >= 0
}

impl BufChannel {
    pub fn with_capacity(cap: i64) -> BufChannel ! BufIoError
        effects [AllocNative]
        requires cap >= 0 && cap <= 1048576 else BufIoError.CapacityOverflow
        ensures result.read_pos == 0 && result.write_pos == 0 && result.buf.cap == cap

    pub fn unread_len(self) -> i64
        effects []
        ensures result == self.write_pos - self.read_pos && result >= 0

    pub fn write_frame(mut self, payload: i64) -> i64 ! BufIoError
        effects [Mutate, AllocNative]
        requires self.write_pos < 1048576 else BufIoError.CapacityOverflow
        ensures self.write_pos == old(self.write_pos) + 1 && result == self.write_pos - self.read_pos

    pub fn read_frame(mut self) -> i64 ! BufIoError
        effects [Mutate]
        requires self.read_pos < self.write_pos else BufIoError.BufferUnderflow
        ensures self.read_pos == old(self.read_pos) + 1

    pub fn compact(mut self) -> i64 ! BufIoError
        effects [Mutate]
        ensures self.read_pos == 0 && self.write_pos == old(self.write_pos) - old(self.read_pos) && result == self.write_pos

    pub fn flush_all(mut self) -> i64
        effects [Mutate]
        ensures self.read_pos == 0 && self.write_pos == 0 && self.flushed_count == old(self.flushed_count) + (old(self.write_pos) - old(self.read_pos)) && result == self.flushed_count

    pub fn drop_channel(mut self) -> i64
        effects [Mutate, AllocNative]
        ensures self.read_pos == 0 && self.write_pos == 0 && self.buf.cap == 0 && result == 0
}

@example("EX-STD-BUFIO-01: BufChannel write_frame, read_frame, compact shift, flush_all, and drop") {
    var ch = BufChannel.with_capacity(4)!
    ch.write_frame(100)!
    ch.write_frame(200)!
    ch.write_frame(300)!
    assert(ch.read_frame()! == 100)
    assert(ch.unread_len() == 2)
    val rem = ch.compact()!
    assert(rem == 2)
    assert(ch.read_pos == 0)
    assert(ch.write_pos == 2)
    assert(ch.read_frame()! == 200)
    assert(ch.flush_all() == 1)
    assert(ch.unread_len() == 0)
    ch.drop_channel()
    assert(active_native_boxes() == 0)
}

@example("EX-STD-BUFIO-02: BufChannel rejects underflow read on empty channel") {
    var ch = BufChannel.with_capacity(2)!
    val e1 = ch.read_frame()
    assert(e1 is Err(BufIoError.BufferUnderflow))
    ch.write_frame(55)!
    assert(ch.read_frame()! == 55)
    val e2 = ch.read_frame()
    assert(e2 is Err(BufIoError.BufferUnderflow))
    ch.drop_channel()
    assert(active_native_boxes() == 0)
}
```
